// blaze, the film: one minute at 60 fps for X (3,600 frames), in six shots. Written as data: each shot is a file of
// flecs script (the app's own ui.* prims on the app's tokens), every motion a `Cue`, every sound a `voice.*` event, and
// every number on screen a row of data.json beside it (harness-video turns it into the d_* constants; no number is
// typed into a scene, so re-measuring rerenders the film).
//
//   cd crates/harness
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs blaze-film.mp4 x-landscape-1080p60    # the film, read back
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs frames/ 2.0                           # a still every 2 s
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs blaze-film.wav                        # the mix alone
//   harness-video harness-video/scene/blaze/film.flecs sounds                                # every sound event
//
// Storyboard (cuts.flecs has the times; a shot's file has its motion and its sound):
//
//   shot  seconds      file            what the viewer should feel and learn
//   1     0.0 - 3.6    wait.flecs      The problem, before 4 s: an agent's edit is quick, then it waits for the compiler.
//                                      The loop is typed out and stalls on "wait". Feel: recognition.
//   2     3.6 - 7.2    name.flecs      "The edit loop is the product." Then the name, struck: blaze, a Rust compiler
//                                      and build system built for coding agents. Feel: a claim, plainly made.
//   3     7.2 - 19.0   what.flecs      What it is, seven cards, fast then slower (1.5 s each to 1.9 s): a resident
//                                      daemon; results keyed by code identity; sandboxed build scripts and proc macros;
//                                      byte-identical outputs; its own linker patching the running binary; optimizer
//                                      rewrites checked in Lean (labelled in progress); `blaze debug inspect`. Learn:
//                                      what is different about it. Each card lands a note higher.
//   4     19.0 - 31.5  loop.flecs      The edit loop, visceral: a line is typed; the grid of cached results lights; the
//                                      figure "cached results re-verified per body edit" counts to its before, then
//                                      falls to its after as the dots go dark, leaving the few an edit still touches
//                                      (the data's own share). A rise, ticks quickening, one hit where it lands. Then
//                                      the day's other three before-and-after rows. Feel: the work disappearing.
//   5     31.5 - 50.5  race.flecs,     Head to head with Relax (makepad's Rust JIT), a race a row: three rows where
//                      behind.flecs    blaze is ahead, then, under "Where blaze is behind today", the four where it is
//                                      not, at the same scale and in the same colours. Conditions in the small print
//                                      the whole shot. Learn: exactly where it stands; trust the numbers because the
//                                      bad ones are there.
//   6     50.5 - 60.0  end.flecs       The mark catches fire; the line again; github.com/indexable-inc/blaze; what is
//                                      still in progress, said so. Fades to the ground it started on.
//
// Honesty (the repository's rule: claims from evidence): a comparison is a measured row of data.json with its conditions
// on screen; rows where blaze is behind are shown as they are; nothing is compared with cargo or rustc (no such row
// exists); nothing says "fastest". What is designed but not built is on the end card as "in progress".
//
// Sound: synthesised by harness-native-blaze's `sound` from the events in the shot files (`harness-video ... sounds`
// lists them), one bed under the whole film, brought to the root's `Mix`. X autoplays muted: the picture carries
// everything, the sound only adds.
include cuts
include tokens
include parts
include wait
include name
include what
include loop
include race
include behind
include end

@tree ChildOf
film : ui.ZStack {
  Video: {width: 960, height: 540, fps: 60, seconds: $t_out, scale: 2}
  // -16 LUFS integrated, no true peak over -1 dBTP: loud enough on a phone, with headroom for X's re-encode.
  Mix: {lufs: -16, peak: -1}
  Fill: $tone_ground
  Flex: {axis: Z, gap: 0, align: Center, justify: Center, wrap: false}
  Size: {w: {kind: Fixed, value: 960, min: 0, max: 0}, h: {kind: Fixed, value: 540, min: 0, max: 0}}
  // The bed: a low warm chord on A under the whole film (its root at 110 Hz, so a phone's speaker still carries it).
  bed : voice.Pad { Onset: {at: 0}; Lasts: {dur: $t_out}; Pitch: {hz: 110}; Gain: {amp: 0.02} }
}
